.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-cartridge 1  "tapectl-cartridge " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-cartridge \- Manage physical cartridges
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl cartridge\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage physical cartridges
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it (issue #241)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept (issue #147)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-register(1)
Register a physical cartridge
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-list(1)
List cartridges
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-info(1)
Show cartridge details
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-move(1)
Move a cartridge to a location, taking its volumes with it
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-retire(1)
Retire a cartridge permanently — it must never be written again
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-mark\-erased(1)
Mark a cartridge as erased (available for reuse)
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-edit(1)
Correct a registered cartridge\*(Aqs generation and/or its claimed serial
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-relabel(1)
Correct a cartridge\*(Aqs barcode label
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-unretire(1)
Reverse a `cartridge retire` — the operator saying they were wrong about the *medium*, not that its bytes are gone
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-journal(1)
Show the MAM journal: every MAM read taken of a cartridge, verbatim
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
